        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Self-Strengthening Movement</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing China</a>: the court and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zongli-yamen">Zongli Yamen</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, and the provincial governments of the lower Yangzi, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a>, Zhili and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hubei">Hubei</a>, with arsenals and shipyards at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuzhou">Fuzhou</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tianjin">Tianjin</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1861–1895: from the creation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zongli-yamen">Zongli Yamen</a> after the Second Opium War to defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>; often divided into phases of arms and schools (1861–1872), enterprises for wealth (1872–1885) and industry and naval building (1885–1895)</span></div>
